/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T12:54:36-08:00","id":16739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drecain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/8938-anyone-getting-baldurs-gate-2-enhanced-editon?p=9649#post9649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of user mods? New gear and classes or even new locations and questlines?</div> </div> </div> </div>The BiG World Project is the biggest &quot;megamod&quot; in the Baldur's Gate modding community: a collection of hundreds of mods released in the last decade that expand upon the basic game. Due to the sheer volume of mods, it can also be somewhat confusing if you're new to the game. There's also the BiG World Setup, which is an automated program that downloads and installs the mods for you.<br /> <br /> There's also GemRB, which is an in-development clone of the Infinity engine (the engine BG runs on) that is being written so people can make their own games with a similar style. Furthermore, GemRB also (partially right now) supports the assets of the BG games, so you can use it to run BG (partly right now). The main benefit of GemRB is that it will remove the hardcoded limitations of the infinity engine, such as the limit on the number of people in your party. I'm still waiting until GemRB is complete and the BiG World Project is made compatible with it, so that I can finally play BG with all the party members at once (including members added by mods).<br /> <br /> There's also Baldur's Gate Reloaded, a mod for Neverwinter Nights 2 that remakes Baldur's Gate in glorious 3D graphics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}